Thank you all. I have already got the answer from your replies. 

<p>I know that I can't take reference to the return value of a subroutine directly. But I want to know why? Here is an example.</p>

<code>
sub foo{
  return (0, 1);
}

my $var = \(foo());  # $var is not a reference to the array (0, 1). 
</code>
